Installing GImageView (GTK 4 port)
==================================

The GTK 4 port is built with Meson; the old configure script (autoconf /
automake) is gone.


Requirements
------------

 * GTK >= 4.10, GLib >= 2.72, gdk-pixbuf 2.0
 * Meson, Ninja, a C compiler and pkg-config (to build)
 * Tested on the X Window System (X11).  On Wayland, the MPlayer and xine
   plugins cannot embed movie playback.

Optional, each enables a feature when found:

 * libarchive     archives (zip, rar, 7z, lha, tar, ...)
 * libjpeg        faster JPEG loading
 * libexif        EXIF viewer and EXIF orientation
 * librsvg        SVG
 * libmng         MNG
 * libwmf         WMF
 * GStreamer 1.16 movie and audio playback (gstreamer, gst-plugins-base)
 * xine-lib 1.2   movie and audio playback
 * mplayer        movie and audio playback (the program, at run time)
 * gettext        translations


Building and installing
-----------------------

In the top source directory:

    $ meson setup _build --prefix=/usr/local
    $ ninja -C _build
    $ sudo ninja -C _build install

To uninstall:

    $ sudo ninja -C _build uninstall


Options
-------

Pass them to meson setup as -Doption=value (see meson_options.txt), or
change them later with meson configure _build -Doption=value.

    nls      (true)   translations
    exif     (auto)   EXIF viewer (system libexif)
    splash   (true)   splash window on startup
                      (it can also be turned off in the preferences)
    jpeg     (auto)   libjpeg based JPEG loader plugin
    mng      (auto)   MNG loader plugin
    svg      (auto)   SVG loader plugin
    wmf      (auto)   WMF loader plugin
    libarchive (auto) archive plugin
    gstreamer (auto)  GStreamer movie plugin
    mplayer  (true)   MPlayer movie plugin
    xine     (auto)   xine movie plugin

"auto" enables a feature when its library is found; "enabled" makes a
missing library an error.  Example:

    $ meson setup _build -Dxine=enabled -Dsvg=enabled -Dexif=enabled


Debian package
--------------

    $ sudo apt build-dep ./       (or install the Build-Depends of debian/control)
    $ dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
    $ sudo apt install ../gimageview_*.deb


Help documents
--------------

The documents opened from the Help menu are installed in
$prefix/share/gimageview/doc/html/<language> and
$prefix/share/gimageview/doc/text/<language> (ja and en).  The language of
the messages (LANGUAGE, LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, LANG) chooses them; languages
without documents get the English ones.
